     unique and alphabetically ordered. They come from ALL edges — changing the
     start doesn't narrow the options list, only the diagram. */

/* `loadNodeColors()` pushes the source WITHOUT a type and the destination WITH
     a type, keeping the first occurrence: a node that was already born as a
     source is `Regular`. */

/* `.datepicker-wrapper`: fs-14 semi-bold label and the `bds-datepicker
            type-of-date="period"` — two "De"/"Até" `bds-input`s with the
            `calendar` icon. Their floating calendar becomes the native picker. */

/* `Ix` › `jx` › `Ax` (title) and `Zx` (the secondary "Atualizar" button with
            `refresh`). Atualizar resubmits the filter as-is — that's `te()` →
            `K()`. */

